cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MAVER: A Multi-Agent Framework for Verification and Experience-Informed Recovery of Microservices"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Yifeng
    affiliation: The University of Melbourne
repository-code: "https://github.com/evenodderguy/maver"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  MAVER diagnoses and repairs live Kubernetes microservice incidents with a pipeline of
  typed roles driven by a privately served open-weight language model. Diagnosis and
  planning are read-only; a single execution role holds every write-capable tool and
  applies its plan under a check-and-set discipline behind a stage-aware approval gate.
  Optional mechanisms add an independent verification role that can hand work back and
  a gated second diagnostic opinion informed by an experience store of past incidents.
keywords:
  - incident response
  - site reliability engineering
  - kubernetes
  - large language model agents
  - retrieval-augmented generation
